  "statistics_amendment": "The planned nucleolar/nucleoplasm analyses could not be saved: the workspace refuses cohorts of compartment revisions until every parent nucleus has a resolved candidate state (assert_complete_compartments), and the NPM1 Cellpose-SAM detection left unresolved parents (no_candidate / indeterminate / review_required) in every field, including all parents of one ActD field. Excluding those nuclei would select cells by the outcome, so the saved statistics use the nuclear region set instead. The change was made because of this software gate, before any statistical result was computed; the nucleolar masks and their per-parent states remain visible in the image view.",
  "grid_notes": "Nuclei: full 3 x 3 grid of StarDist probability (0.4/0.5/0.6) and NMS (0.2/0.3/0.4) at the automatic detection scale on all fields. The default marker definition is computed in the browser for any nuclear result. NCL-positive alternatives (Cellpose-SAM 4.3.0 with default settings, one CPU inference 1.5-18 min per field; Fiji NCL threshold with default settings) are recorded on all fields for the default nuclear result only; after changing the nuclear setting they report showcase_detection_not_recorded. Cellpose-SAM cell ROI is not recorded: the dataset has no cell-boundary or cytoplasmic channel."
 },
